// Original V51 campaign prose. Generated by Author-CampaignV51.py.
WFV51_MESSAGE("B.Order2","四月的残骸仍横在布勒库尔铁丝前，澳军再次投入进攻。枪榴弹压住胸墙，步兵夺取中央补给湾，接通送弹道路。","April's wreckage remains before the Bullecourt wire as the Australians attack again. Rifle grenades cover the parapet; infantry must take the central stores and open the ammunition route.")
WFV51_MESSAGE("G.Order2","澳军重返布勒库尔，枪榴弹正落向兴登堡线。守住中央补给湾，以分散枪位封锁铁丝缺口。","The Australians return to Bullecourt. Rifle grenades fall on the Hindenburg Line. Hold the central stores and cover the wire gaps from separated gun posts.")
WFV51_MESSAGE("B.Order4","山脊上的新胸墙尚未夯实，东面的反击已经逼近。机枪守住接近线，预备队接应中央阵位。","The new parapets on the ridge are still loose. A counterattack approaches from the east. Guns must hold the approaches, with reserves within reach of the centre.")
WFV51_MESSAGE("G.Order4","梅西讷失守两日，反击命令送到前沿。沿坑岸向中央推进；英军预备队仍在高地后方集结。","Two days after Messines falls, the counterattack order reaches the front. Advance along the crater rims towards the centre. British reserves are gathering beyond the ridge.")
WFV51_MESSAGE("B.Order5","皮尔克姆的排水沟已被炮击切断，送弹队挤上残存木板路。壕炮先到，野炮仍陷在后方；逐个压住湿地中的枪位。","Shellfire has severed the Pilckem drains. Ammunition parties crowd the surviving duckboards. Trench mortars arrive ahead of the field batteries; work through the flooded gun posts in turn.")
WFV51_MESSAGE("G.Order5","雨水漫过皮尔克姆的旧弹坑。携弹队先把壕炮弹背到前沿，机枪沿尚可通行的硬地换位。","Rain fills the old shell holes at Pilckem. Bearers bring mortar bombs forward first. Move the machine guns along the remaining firm approaches.")
WFV51_MESSAGE("B.Order6","朗厄马尔克的农场只剩混凝土残墙。迫击炮弹正送往前沿补给湾；夺下补给，压住相互照应的枪位。","Concrete walls are all that remain of the Langemarck farms. Mortar bombs are moving to the forward stores. Take the supply bay and silence the supporting gun posts.")
WFV51_MESSAGE("G.Order6","积水把朗厄马尔克的据点分隔开，中央送弹路仍可通行。守住补给湾，掩护各枪组换防。","Floodwater separates the Langemarck posts, but the central ammunition route remains open. Hold the stores and cover the relief of each gun crew.")
WFV51_MESSAGE("B.Order10","冬夜巡逻只带轻装装备。沿低地接近前哨，烟幕掩护暴露地段；本次没有装甲、重炮与机队支援。","The winter patrol travels light. Approach the outpost through low ground and cover exposed stretches with smoke. Armour, heavy guns and aircraft are unavailable.")
WFV51_MESSAGE("G.Order10","铁丝前留下了新脚印，前哨尚未回话。轻装分队沿低地接近，烟幕掩护通路；重炮与装甲没有配属。","Fresh tracks stop before the wire. The outpost has not answered. Light sections move through the low ground under smoke cover; heavy guns and armour are not attached.")
WFV51_MESSAGE("B.Order11","三月二十一日，米夏埃尔攻势冲破浓雾。第五集团军正在后撤，本连须接通被截断的道路，掩护失散部队归队。","On 21 March, Operation Michael breaks through the fog. Fifth Army withdraws. Reopen the severed road and cover the return of isolated troops.")
WFV51_MESSAGE("G.Order11","米夏埃尔攻势的炮火向纵深延伸。突击队穿过雾中缺口，A7V 与机枪跟进；中央补给湾关系到后续攻势。","The guns of Operation Michael lift deeper. Assault parties pass through gaps in the fog, followed by A7Vs and machine guns. The central stores sustain the advance.")
WFV51_MESSAGE("B.Order14","八月八日清晨，澳大利亚与加拿大部队在亚眠以东推进，法军攻击南侧。坦克随步兵出发，炮火切断守军增援。","At dawn on 8 August, Australians and Canadians advance east of Amiens while the French attack farther south. Tanks move with the infantry; shellfire cuts off the defenders' reinforcements.")
WFV51_MESSAGE("G.Order14","亚眠的前沿接连失去联络。缴获坦克与 Tankgewehr 组抵达，机枪掩护后卫；为撤出的部队重新打开交通。","Forward posts at Amiens fall out of contact. Captured tanks and Tankgewehr teams arrive under the rearguard's machine guns. Reopen communications for the withdrawing troops.")
WFV51_MESSAGE("B.Order16","里克瓦尔的运河明渠横在前方。工兵沿破损坡岸接近，法军喷火分遣队清理近处掩体；烟幕掩护渡越。","The open canal cutting at Riqueval lies ahead. Engineers approach along the broken banks; a French flame detachment clears nearby cover while smoke screens the crossing.")
WFV51_MESSAGE("G.Order16","运河纤道仍能通行，两侧枪位保持联络。工兵照看通路，预备队准备夺回失守的中央阵位。","The canal towpath remains open and the bank guns are still in contact. Pioneers tend the route; reserves stand ready to retake the centre if it falls.")
WFV51_MESSAGE("B.Order17","塞勒河切口里的列车仍在掩护撤运。工兵清出接近线，反装甲火力打击车载枪炮，步兵沿路堤展开。","A train in the Selle cutting covers the evacuation. Pioneers clear the approach, anti-armour fire engages the rail guns and infantry spread along the embankment.")
WFV51_MESSAGE("G.Order17","塞勒河车站仍在装车，列车炮组留在切口。步兵掩护车载枪炮的侧翼，守住通往河岸的道路。","Loading continues at the Selle station while the train guns hold the cutting. Infantry cover their flanks and hold the road to the riverbank.")
WFV51_MESSAGE("B.Order19","十一月四日，新西兰部队逼近勒凯努瓦城墙。桑布尔渡口仍在交火；肃清后沿，掩护后续部队通过。城郊禁止毒气与空中轰炸。","On 4 November, New Zealand troops approach the walls of Le Quesnoy. Fighting continues at the Sambre crossings. Clear the rear for the following troops. Gas and aerial bombing are prohibited near the town.")
WFV51_MESSAGE("G.Order19","南方停战的电报已到，西线仍在开火。机枪守住桑布尔渡口，预备队掩护最后的通路。城郊禁止毒气与空中轰炸。","News of the southern armistice has arrived. The Western Front still fires. Machine guns hold the Sambre crossing while reserves cover the last route. Gas and aerial bombing are prohibited near the town.")
WFV51_MESSAGE("Record","战役终章","CAMPAIGN EPILOGUE")
WFV51_MESSAGE("Title","炮声止息之时","THE GUNS FALL SILENT")
WFV51_MESSAGE("Date","1918年11月11日 · 上午11时","11 NOVEMBER 1918 · 11 A.M.")
WFV51_MESSAGE("British.Subtitle","从阿拉斯到桑布尔","FROM ARRAS TO THE SAMBRE")
WFV51_MESSAGE("German.Subtitle","漫长的归途","THE LONG ROAD HOME")
WFV51_MESSAGE("British.End1","十一月十一日上午十一时，西线停火。消息沿电话线传到连部，前沿的枪声逐渐止息。士兵爬上壕沿，身后的担架队还在行走。","At eleven on 11 November, the Western Front ceasefire takes effect. The news reaches the company by telephone. Men climb onto the parapet as stretcher parties continue behind them.")
WFV51_MESSAGE("British.End2","连队清点生还者，把未归队者记入名册。桑布尔之后的行军结束了，归乡命令尚未送到。","The company musters its survivors and records the missing. The march beyond the Sambre is over. Orders for home have yet to arrive.")
WFV51_MESSAGE("German.End1","十一月十一日上午十一时，停战生效。枪炮沉寂，德军开始准备撤出占领区。连队在撤退道路旁重新集合。","At eleven on 11 November, the armistice takes effect. The guns fall silent as German troops prepare to leave the occupied territories. The company assembles beside the withdrawal road.")
WFV51_MESSAGE("German.End2","军士念完名册，在缺席者的名字旁留下记号。士兵收起武器，等待归途上的下一道命令。","The NCO finishes the roll, marking the names of the absent. Rifles are stowed. The men wait for the next order on the road home.")
